# XTNL dead-man receiver watchdog (home receiver VPS, home-server-plan §3.1, W6): /etc/xtnl/deadman-healthz.env,
# 0600 root:root (systemd reads it as root; xtnl-deadman-healthz.service runs as a dynamic user and never logs it).
#     sudo install -m 0600 -o root -g root /dev/null /etc/xtnl/deadman-healthz.env && sudoedit /etc/xtnl/deadman-healthz.env
# Runbook: docs/runbooks/deadman-receiver-home.md.

# Healthchecks.io check B ("receiver or VPS down"; period 1 min, grace 3 min), the full ping URL
# (https://hc-ping.com/<uuid>). A SECRET: anyone holding it can keep check B green. Never reuse check A's URL (the
# engine's XTNL_HEARTBEAT_COPY_URL) or check C's (backups): each check proves one thing. The unit appends /fail
# when /healthz does not answer 200.
XTNL_HEALTHZ_PING_URL=CHANGE_ME

# The receiver's /healthz (default http://127.0.0.1:8443/healthz, the XTNL_RECEIVER_LISTEN of the home receiver).
# XTNL_HEALTHZ_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8443/healthz
